## TASK
Implement exactly six missing or incorrect runtime bridge functions according to the GPT-fixed interface. Keep the candidate disabled.

## FILES
Return replacements only for FinishMonitor methods in First_Phase/scene_demo/finish_v1/runtime.py: _check, poll, _finish_outcome, status, close, _collect_observations.
Forbidden: other methods, control, sensors, vision, tests, prior evidence, Git, credentials, simulation, physical actions or image API calls. Actual DeepSeek supplies implementation, GPT decides and accepts, a local worker applies the replacements.

## STEPS
1. Return one bare JSON object {"functions":{"_check":"complete def source", "poll":"complete def source", "_finish_outcome":"complete def source", "status":"complete def source", "close":"complete def source", "_collect_observations":"complete def source"}}. Each value starts with def at column zero, includes its complete body, no class indentation. Do not repeat old code, generate other functions, add markdown, or explain. Output budget 3600 tokens.
2. _collect_observations(self, extra_observations): merged={float(cap['timestamp']):cap for cap in list(self.history)+list(extra_observations or [])+[self.port.capture()]}; selected=[merged[t] for t in sorted(merged)[-3:]]; clear and extend self.history with selected; return selected. Fresh capture must override older same-timestamp entries. Capture failure or missing timestamp raises; do not swallow.
3. _check(self, context, observations): selected=self._collect_observations(observations). For each selected cap use verification_frames when nonempty, otherwise frames. Use at most TWO frames per timestamp, append paths and sensor_frames together, frame=len(paths) before append, view=fr['view'], timestamp=float(cap['timestamp']). sensor_frames have only frame/view/timestamp, paths are fr['rgb_path']; maximum six total, raise if exceeding six rather than independently truncate or dedup paths. Each timestamp has at most two views. robot=self.port.read_robot(); measurements contain ONLY stage=(self.port.phase or 'post_execution'), finger_qpos=[float(x) for x in robot['finger_qpos']] (must be two), max_abs_arm_qvel=max(abs(float(x)) for x in robot['arm_qvel']), standard_open_finger_qpos=[float(x) for x in self.reference['finger_home']] (must be two). This standard open is actual encoder calibration, not oracle. Safe ctx keys ONLY user_request/current_subtask/criteria (from context argument), sensor_frames, actuator_measurements. Never send gold/native/truth/arm_qpos/contacts/robot. If self.calls>=10 raise. Set self._phase='visual_check'. guarded_step(lambda:None) immediately before and after API. Increment calls once before actual self.call_client.analyze(ctx,paths), no retry. Returned meta is a top-level dict, raw=meta['verdict']; fused=vision.reconcile_verdict(context,raw,robot,self.reference); self._last_decision=vision.decide(context,fused). _write_check stores raw_verdict, verdict, meta usage/status/model/http_status/request_sha256/response_sha256/call_index, image paths, sensor_frames, ctx and measured robot separately (numpy serializer already exists). Return fused. All errors propagate. Use real module scene_demo.finish_v1.vision via lazy import.
4. poll(self, step, candidate=False, force=False): return existing terminal. Compute first_candidate=bool(candidate) and not self.last_candidate BEFORE assigning last_candidate. Only check when at least two distinct history timestamps, self.prechecks<5, and step>=next_due OR first_candidate OR force. Insufficient timestamps do not consume candidate edge. After successful _check, assign self.last_candidate=bool(candidate), increment prechecks, next_due=step+self.interval. Use self._last_decision from _check. incomplete sets _phase='observing' and returns None. unknown -> _finish_outcome(False,'visual_unknown'). Only needs_release/needs_retreat/complete may invoke original control.run_finish(self.port,self.context,verdict,vision.decide,self._check,emit=lambda _:None) once; invalid state raises. Save self._finish. Immediately after run_finish call guarded_step(lambda:None), because run_finish may catch cancellation. finish['ok'] and independent_streak>=5 -> _finish_outcome(True,'complete'); finish ok but streak<5 -> independent_finish_failed; otherwise preserve finish.reason or independent_finish_failed. All failures close then raise, not swallow. Never hold service lock over API: guard probes acquire it only briefly. Continuously true candidate must not check on every action. Do not change controller algorithms.
5. _finish_outcome(self, ok, reason): set terminal with bool ok, str reason, checks=self.calls, optional finish=self._finish when not None; self.close(); return terminal.
6. status(self): JSON-safe dict phase: terminal true=>'done', false=>'blocked'; else if _phase=='visual_check' use visual_check, otherwise self.port.phase or self._phase. Include calls/prechecks/helper_counts copy/last_decision copy or None/terminal only ok,reason,checks (no full finish or numpy)/independent_streak. close(self): idempotent, call self.port.close(), mark closed after success; exceptions propagate.

## INTERFACE
FinishMonitor already has self.reference/context/history(deque maxlen3)/port/guarded_step/call_client/calls/prechecks/next_due/interval/last_candidate/terminal/independent_streak/helper_counts/_last_decision/_closed/_finish/_phase='observing'. SensorPort lives in scene_demo.finish_v1.sensors, has capture()->dict(timestamp,frames, optional verification_frames), read_robot()->dict(finger_qpos,arm_qvel,etc), phase string or None, close(). self._write_check(row) already writes UTF8 LF and serializes numpy arrays; never reimplement it. self.call_client is scene_demo.finish_v1.vision.QwenClient; analyze(ctx,image_paths)->top-level dict(verdict,usage,status,model,http_status,request_sha256,response_sha256,call_index). vision.reconcile_verdict(context,verdict,robot,reference)->dict, vision.decide(context,verdict)->dict(state,reason,allow_release,allow_retreat). control.run_finish(port,context,initial_verdict,decide_fn,check_fn,emit)->dict. Its exact existing implementation must stay unchanged.

## DONE WHEN
Exactly the six requested function names are present and each source parses as one function, worker applies unique class AST line ranges then whole module ast.parse passes. paths and frame metadata have identical length and continuous global indices. Standard-open calibration present. Repeated candidate is edge-triggered and all cancellation probes remain. JSON-safe status, no API/physical/test/Git runs. Wait for GPT software acceptance; do not claim chain verified.

## REPORT
Only the specified bare JSON functions object, no prose or additional mappings.


